# Opening a port by device name (Phase 8, fake device): the first port
# in the list whose label contains the name, ignoring case. Labels are
# plain ASCII (a byte outside 32..126 shows as ?), and a name is matched
# against the label as listed. No match is "no such port"; a malformed
# hw: name, or an empty one, is "not understood". The name is looked up
# again at every open, so a device that comes back as another card is
# found again, including when reopening after a lost port.
fakedev port 1 0 2
fakedev port 3 0 1
fakedev name 3 U2MIDI Pro
fakedev port 5 0 1
fakedev name 5 Caf\xe9 Synth
ports
# a name, in either case (the library folds A-Z itself)
open device u2midi
close
open device U2MIDI PRO
fakedev log
close
# a subdevice's own name: the second port of card 1
open device midi 0-1
fakedev log
close
# several match: the first in the list (hw:1,0,0)
open device fake
fakedev log
close
# only the first match is tried: busy, though hw:1,0,1 is free
fakedev busy 1 0 0
open device fake
fakedev free 1 0 0
# ? in a name is only itself
open device caf? synth
close
open device caf?? synth
open device nothing like it
devdiag
# the hw: form as before, now in either case; a malformed one
open device HW:3,0,0
close
open device hw:x
open device
fakedev log
# the cable comes back as card 4: the name finds it there
fakedev unplug 3
open device u2midi
fakedev port 4 0 1
fakedev name 4 U2MIDI Pro
open device u2midi
fakedev log
close
# no match while a card can't be read (no permission): that is the
# likelier reason, so "no permission" rather than "no such port"
fakedev deny 1
open device nothing like it
devdiag
open device u2midi
close
# lost while playing, back as card 6: reopening by name finds it, and
# the held note is released there. Tempo 120, a beat is 500 ms; the
# port is lost at beat 2 by 45's note-off, with 60 still sounding.
open device u2midi
track 1 45:2 52:2
track 2 60:4
play continue
sleep 250
fakedev unplug 4
sleep 1000
state
fakedev port 6 0 1
fakedev name 6 U2MIDI Pro
fakedev log
open device u2midi
state
devdiag
close
fakedev log
